              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MrsFisher0729"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for a Thanksgiving potluck. The macadamias and coconut on top did burn. If I made this again I would add both ingredients to the top at the end of the cooking time."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RosySake8159"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made this recipe for years and it has always been a favorite. But I recently found Duncan Hines, Dolly Parton‘s Southern style coconut cake mix, which took it to another level.",
            "datePublished": "2023-10-04T17:28:09.433Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cazzy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "use to make this with the kids when they were pre-teens. Now being a grandmother, I use the French vanilla cake mix with 1/2 c of melted butter, making it a crumbled topping for the top. I use 1 can of crushed pineapple with juice &amp; 2 cans of the cherry pie filling. I bake mine for 50 min. &amp; put pieces of dark chocolate squares on top of the crumbled cake mix at the last 5 min of baking. Over the years we have used different taste variations such as pineapple/apple pie filling with caramel flavor cake mix for a caramel apple taste...",
            "datePublished": "2015-10-05T04:20:03.890Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GeordieTX"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The whole of this dessert is greater than the sum of its parts. A crowd pleaser. I used half the coconut, half the butter, and walnuts instead of macadamias as that is all I had. Came out great.",
            "datePublished": "2022-01-01T21:12:10.107Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Becky"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This might have been good but I saw the same recipe cooked in a crockpot on low for 3 hrs. It was moist and great that way. This was ok but dry compared to the crockpot method.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-18T02:25:33.363Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JJNE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good starter recipe. I had no trouble with the coconut burning. Baked on the medium rack for 50 mins. And kept checking to see the coconut browning and the filling bubbling. Also sprinkled the dry cake mix with cinnamon and a little brown sugar before I added the coconut. Added a small bag of thawed, drained sweet pitted cherries with the pie filling. Everyone liked it.",
            "datePublished": "2016-10-02T00:56:54.980Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Anne Williams Nielsen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this recipe many times (minus the nuts and coconut), 1/2 the butter - sliced thin, rather than melted. I use 2 cans of cherry pie filling rather than 1. And I serve it with a scoop of french vanilla ice cream on top. Quite sweet but very yummy. Kids love it! Next time I make it I am going to try topping it with the coconut and chopped pecans.",
            "datePublished": "2013-10-25T03:02:45.407Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "squeekie56"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this on Christmas 2017. It was good while warm, except everyone thought there were too many nuts (along with the coconut, made it quite crumbly). If I make it again I will only use 1/2 the amount of macadamia nuts.Also feel that the coconut would have been better between pineapple and cake layers OR before melted butter. Lastly, I used 1 can of Lucky Leaf Tart Red Cherries. I think the Pie Filling would have been better although a whole lot sweeter. As made, it had just the right amount of sweetness, but cherries turned unappealing color and texture was off when dessert cooled.",
            "datePublished": "2018-01-07T20:03:36.730Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "VERY good. Put oven at 300 not 350. Used chunk pineapple. When you smell cake cooking and the liquid boiling pop down to 250s to just continue to soften the big pineapples. Sweet coconut and macadamias won't burn that badly then.",
            "datePublished": "2020-07-29T02:54:22.917Z"
          },
